# Caddy on the workload host (review fix 7): terminates :443 so app-server's
# Caddy (`docker/Caddyfile`'s `/api/webhooks*` route) has a real TLS
# endpoint to proxy to. The gateway process (`packages/workload`) binds
# `127.0.0.1:8080` only — it never listens on a public interface itself.
#
# `tls internal` — Caddy's own local CA, not a public CA (ACME/Let's
# Encrypt needs a public DNS name; this host is addressed by IP from
# app-server, behind the cloud firewall's 443-from-app-server-only rule,
# so a public cert buys nothing extra). app-server's Caddyfile pins this
# CA's root explicitly (`tls_trust_pool file`) rather than trusting the
# system store, which would never trust a locally-issued cert. See the
# runbook's Bring-up section for copying the root CA to app-server.
:443 {
	tls internal

	header -Server
	header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
